{"name":"Shaved Ice","hex":"#a9b4ba","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"shaved ice","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various desserts that incorporate finely crushed or shaved ice and a sweet syrup.","The finely crushed ice itself."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shaved_ice"}],"entries":[{"title":"Shaved ice","blocks":[{"text":"Shaved ice is a large family of ice-based desserts made of fine shavings of ice and sweet condiments or flavored syrups. Usually, the syrup is added after the ice has been frozen and shaved—typically at the point of sale; however, flavoring can also be added before freezing. The dessert is consumed worldwide in various forms and ways. Shaved ice can also be mixed with large quantities of liquid to produce shaved ice drinks."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Shavedice.jpg/330px-Shavedice.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shaved_ice"},{"title":"Hawaiian shave ice","blocks":[{"text":"Shave ice or Hawaiian shave ice is an ice-based dessert made by shaving a block of ice and flavoring it with syrup and other sweet ingredients. On Hawai‘i Island, it is also called \"ice shave\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Hilo_Ice_Shave.JPG/330px-Hilo_Ice_Shave.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hawaiian_shave_ice"},{"title":"Ice","blocks":[{"text":"Ice is water that is frozen into a solid state, typically forming at or below temperatures of 0 °C, 32 °F, or 273.15 K. It occurs naturally on Earth, on other planets, in Oort cloud objects, and as interstellar ice. As a naturally occurring crystalline inorganic solid with an ordered structure, ice is considered to be a mineral. Depending on the presence of impurities such as particles of soil or bubbles of air, it can appear transparent or a more or less opaque bluish-white color."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Ice_Block%2C_Canal_Park%2C_Duluth_%2832752478892%29.jpg/330px-Ice_Block%2C_Canal_Park%2C_Duluth_%2832752478892%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ice"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Shavedice.jpg/500px-Shavedice.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Shavedice.jpg/1280px-Shavedice.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Shavedice.jpg/500px-Shavedice.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AShavedice.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Hawaiian_Blizzard_syrup.jpg/500px-Hawaiian_Blizzard_syrup.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Hawaiian_Blizzard_syrup.jpg/500px-Hawaiian_Blizzard_syrup.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Syrups used for flavouring shaved ice","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHawaiian_Blizzard_syrup.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Shave_ice_machine.jpg/500px-Shave_ice_machine.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Shave_ice_machine.jpg/1280px-Shave_ice_machine.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Shave_ice_machine.jpg/500px-Shave_ice_machine.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_c